// Pigment on monochrome levels (M4; docs/milestone-4-plan.md §3.4).
// Schema: `ls_sim::pigment::PigmentSettings`. Times in s.
// A monochrome level (Palette 80+, or any Last Color Standing level) gets pigment pickups at its
// pickup points as its rule set's `pigment_pickup` says (one per `players_per_pickup` players in
// play, at least `min_on_map`, each respawning `respawn_secs` after it was taken; rule set code
// format 5). Touching one colours your ship for `duration_secs`
// (refreshed by another): +`damage_bonus` damage with every weapon, visible to everyone. A
// pigmented ship that dies drops a splash pickup that lasts `splash_secs`. In Last Color Standing
// a pickup restores `restore_colour` colour instead (no damage bonus there).
// Changing a number changes the data hash (handshake).
PigmentSettings(
    duration_secs: 40.0,
    damage_bonus: 0.25,
    splash_secs: 15.0,
    restore_colour: 17,
)
